    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0453" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg357"/>

                <head>No. 182.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Scruggs to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 17, 1874</date>.
                        (Received July 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 39.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have by this mail transmitted to the
                    Department the annual report of the Colombian secretary of foreign affairs to
                    the congress of <pb facs="0454" n="358" xml:id="pg358"/> this country, for the
                    year ending April, 1874. The portion allotted to the discussion of the relations
                    between Colombia and the United States will be found on page 83, paragraph 6,
                    and from thence to page 85 inclusive. A translation of this portion of the
                    report is inclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. L. SCRUGGS.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d184-a1.xml" xpointer="d184-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d184-a2.xml" xpointer="d184-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
